that the final output of the move and halfmove are allowed to be incorrect. So the above is scored properly even though the move numbers are wrong.\n\nWith these exceptions (and only these exceptions) you must implement a fully correct move generator, including:\n- Castling, with proper tracking of castling rights\n- Promotion, except only allow promotion to queen\n- En-passant\n\nThe length of re.json must be under 100,000 [regex, replacement]-pairs long, and under 10 megabytes in total.\n\nYou can look at the provided check.py to verify if your solution is correct. You will be tested on other positions as well.\n"], "completed": true, "concurrent_cells_at_end": 4, "concurrent_cells_at_start": 4, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "embedded_version": "2.0.50", "ended_et": "2026-11-12T18:57:07.710468-05:00", "ended_on_rejection": false, "endpoint_location": "global", "endpoint_location_mixed": false, "env_cause": null, "env_failure": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "failure_subclass": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "final_workspace_bytes": 228279, "final_workspace_skip_reason": null, "final_workspace_status": "saved", "final_workspace_tar": "/h2/drift-5140-1103/opus/5140/transcripts/without/opencode_regex-chess_claude-opus-5-5_trial5.workspace.tar.gz", "final_workspace_tar_bytes": 17185, "final_workspace_tar_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "free_disk_gb": 37.15, "fresh_subagents": 0, "functional_pass": null, "gate_cell": false, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170344 (/h1/opencode-src/bin/<REDACTED_HEX>/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "<HOST>", "image_digest": null, "image_scan_copies": [], "installed_anthropic": "2.0.50", "instance_id": "8187537343833955709", "instruction_app_rewrite": true, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "load_proof": "pass", "load_proof_basis": "user_agent", "load_proof_reason": "User-Agent 2.0.50", "loaded_anthropic": "2.0.50", "lock_wait_s": 0.0, "lockfile": "bun.lock", "lockfile_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "machine": "<HOST>", "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_match_reason": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "network_mode": "local", "off_protocol": false, "opencode_cache": "/h1/opencode-src", "output_tail": "s won't look like this.\n\n**Speed:** each position takes about 1.3 seconds. Most of that is Python recompiling the patterns on every call, because there are far more of them than its regex cache holds. The full `check.py` run took about 16 seconds.\n\n**How it works:**\n1. **Unpack:** the board is written out at a fixed width, with empty squares as `_` and `//` between ranks. Castling rights and the en passant file are stored as digits after it.\n2. **Generate moves:** each rule covers one move geometry, such as one start square to one target square with the squares in between empty. If the move is possible from the original position, the rule adds a new line with the board after that move. Queens, rooks, bishops and the king share rules where their moves overlap. Promotion is always to a queen; en passant is checked against the stored file, and castling against the stored rights.\n3. **Castling safety:** a castling move first places extra king copies on the squares the king passes through. The check filter in the next step then also rejects castling out of or through check.\n4. **Remove illegal moves:** one combined pattern deletes any line where the white king is attacked. The `//` separators stop attack patterns from wrapping around the edge of the board.\n5. **Pack back into FEN:** castling rights are cleared when the king or a rook has left (or been captured on) its starting square. The output then gets `b`, the castling field, the en passant field and `0 0`.\n\nAfter 